 {
   "id": "grammar.b2.argentinaba.05.estructuras-conjeturales-metafisicas",
-  "title": "Estructuras conjeturales y metafísicas en la literatura fantástica",
+  "title": "The Future of Probability: Guessing About Now",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "La literatura fantástica rioplatense (Borges, Cortázar, Bioy Casares) emplea complejas estructuras conjeturales para difuminar los límites entre realidad, sueño, memoria y laberinto. Destacan construcciones comparativo-hipotéticas con *como si + imperfecto/pluscuamperfecto de subjuntivo*, locuciones de probabilidad conjetural (*cabría inferir que*, *pareciera ser que*) y oraciones modales de apariencia."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know *estará* for a guess about the present from B1 Unit 22: the future tense can express a guess about the present. *Estará en casa* means \"He is probably at home\". When you talk about writers read all over the world, you often cannot give exact figures, so you guess."
     },
     {
       "type": "table",
-      "title": "Estructuras conjeturales en la ficción metafísica",
+      "title": "Guessing with the future",
       "rows": [
         [
-          "El protagonista contemplaba el sótano como si en ese punto microscópico convergiera el universo entero.",
-          "The protagonist contemplated the cellar as if the entire universe converged in that microscopic point."
+          "Habrá alguien comprando un libro de Borges.",
+          "*habrá* + gerund: someone is probably buying one now"
         ],
         [
-          "Cabría inferir que el laberinto no era de piedra sino de líneas trazadas por el destino.",
-          "One might infer that the labyrinth was not made of stone but of lines drawn by fate."
